# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.
#
# Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API Keys
#
# Use a SECRET key (sb_secret_...). Supabase's newer key system replaces the
# legacy JWT keys, which are deprecated at the end of 2026; secret keys can also
# be revoked and rotated one at a time, where rotating service_role means
# rotating the project JWT secret and invalidating everything at once.
#
# The legacy service_role key still works here if that is what your project
# shows — both are accepted, since supabase-js treats them identically.
#
# You do NOT need a publishable key. That one replaces `anon` and is for
# browser-side clients; this app has none. Every query runs in a Server
# Component or Server Action, which is also why migrations/001_init.sql enables
# RLS with no policies.
#
# This key bypasses row level security. It is read only in server-side code
# (lib/supabase.ts imports `server-only`, so the build fails if a Client
# Component ever imports it) and is never shipped to the browser. Neither name
# is prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_, which is what stops Next.js from inlining them
# into the client bundle.

SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...
